10. Join Example
class MyThread extends Thread {
    public void run() {
        System.out.println("Child thread");
    }
}

public class Test {
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        MyThread t = new MyThread();
        t.start();
        t.join();
        System.out.println("Main thread");
    }
}

Output
Child thread
Main thread

11. Synchronization (🔥 VERY IMPORTANT)
Problem: Race Condition
class Counter {
    int count = 0;

    void increment() {
        count++;
    }
}

❌ Not thread-safe

11.1 Synchronized Method
class Counter {
    int count = 0;

    synchronized void increment() {
        count++;
    }
}

✔ Only one thread at a time
✔ Uses object-level lock

11.2 Synchronized Block (Better)
synchronized(this) {
    count++;
}

✔ Fine-grained locking
✔ Better performance

12. Object-Level vs Class-Level Lock
synchronized(this)        // object lock
synchronized(ClassName.class) // class lock

13. Inter-Thread Communication (🔥)
wait(), notify(), notifyAll()
class Shared {
    synchronized void produce() throws Exception {
        System.out.println("Producing...");
        wait();
        System.out.println("Resumed");
    }

    synchronized void consume() {
        System.out.println("Consuming...");
        notify();
    }
}

14. Deadlock (🔥 Must Explain)
Example
synchronized(A) {
    synchronized(B) {}
}

Another thread:

synchronized(B) {
    synchronized(A) {}
}

👉 Both wait forever

Prevention
Avoid nested locks
Use consistent lock order
Use tryLock()

